title HUNK43 — the input seam: a keeper's raw gesture drives the cursor
prompt Continue the autonomous loop — take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, send each finished increment as its own signed round, stop only at custody gates.
think After HUNK42 landed and sent, the next crux its recommend named is the input seam: the boundary above HUNK40's pure cursor that turns a raw gesture (a signed scroll delta, a page/edge key) into exactly one cursor move.
think Lindy weight: every scroll surface has this seam, and it composes HUNK40 exactly rather than inventing anything — durable and agent-doable, no gate touched.
think Designed apply(cursor, input) over an Input { kind, lines } record; scroll routes by sign to line_down/line_up with the magnitude capped at the library count. The one real hazard is i32 min: negating it in i32 overflows, so magnitude() takes the absolute value in i64 before capping into u32 — an assert names the non-negativity.
obs Kept one value model (enum tag + signed count), no new refusal, no storage — the seam only routes to HUNK40's already-clamped gestures, so every clamp guarantee is inherited, not re-proven.
obs The witness red from HUNK39/40/42 recurred a third time (the GREEN line's apostrophe in cursor's breaks the shell single-quoted grep) — dropped the apostrophe from the print line before running, so the witness passed first build. This pattern is now reflexive on this ladder.
obs The selftest drives the cursor by i32 max/min deltas, a zero delta, and a long mixed stream of wheel deltas and page keys, asserting a real viewport after each — an adversarial input can never move the offset off the ends.
loom witness=hunk_scroll_input_witness viewport=2x5 max_offset=3 clamp_deltas=i32min,i32max mixed_stream=8
file pond/apps/preset_scroll_input.rye HUNK43 — apply(cursor, input) routes a raw event to one HUNK40 gesture; magnitude taken in i64 so i32 min never wraps.
file tools/hunk_scroll_input_witness.rish proves the seam on metal — reversible walk, extreme-delta clamp without wrap, page/edge kinds matching the cursor, a fitting library that never moves.
